*** CALICO VERSION UPGRADE ***
1. Install method: confirmed
No calico-system or tigera-operator namespace appeared, so this is a plain manifest install, not the operator.
DATASTORE_TYPE: kubernetes, so there’s no separate etcd for Calico.
Your settings are all defaults: IPIP Always, VXLAN Never, BGP via BIRD, IP autodetect, no Typha. The pod CIDR isn’t set in the DaemonSet, and your pod IPs (192.168.x.x) match Calico’s default range.

That means the standard calico.yaml manifest upgrade fits you, and you have no custom settings to carry over.

Felix (policy and dataplane) is healthy. Your logs show endpoints coming up normally.
BIRD (the BGP daemon that shares routes between nodes) on selfhosted-runner-1 isn’t responding, so that node may not learn route changes properly.

The old pod had been running since January 2026, and its BIRD process had hung, so the readiness probe kept failing for months. A new pod means a new BIRD process, and the sockets in /var/run/calico/ were recreated at 11:48. The Felix half was always fine. A restart is the standard fix for a stuck process.




